## 6.2 Encoder and timeout variables

```cpp
int encoder_cpr_{450};

int serial_timeout_ms_{500};

int boot_wait_ms_{2000};
```

These represent:

**`encoder_cpr_`**

Encoder counts per revolution.

The current default is 450.

However, this value must represent the actual counts per **wheel revolution**, including gearbox reduction and the encoder counting method. It should not automatically be assumed correct because an earlier encoder test displayed approximately 450 counts.

**`serial_timeout_ms_`**

Maximum permitted time without valid wheel telemetry while the hardware is active.

Current value:

500 milliseconds.

**`boot_wait_ms_`**

Time allowed for the Arduino to restart after opening the serial connection.

Current value:

2000 milliseconds.

