```

represents the elapsed duration between control-loop iterations.

### Override

```cpp
override
```

Indicates that this function overrides a virtual function declared in the parent class.

The compiler checks that the function signature matches a suitable function in the base class.

This helps prevent mistakes.

Your implementation currently does not use the `time` or `period` arguments, which is why the `.cpp` definitions leave them unnamed.

